MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_001: Hm? I know you. You are the maiden who\naccompanied the bride.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_002: Oh, uh, hi! How are you?
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_003: Um, nice weather we're having, huh?
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_004: You seem quite anxious. I assure you, you have done\nnothing to offend.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_005: I heard that the people of Saramis are really strong\nwarriors, so I'm trying to be extra polite...
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_006: You need not fear. As a citizen of Saramis, I was\nraised to be an honorable man.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_007: Do not provoke us, and you shall find us people\nof good cheer.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_008: I, uh, I see!
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_009: Still, when I'm near you, I get pretty nervous...
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_010: You're tall, and you've got that scary angry glare,\nand, and...a scary beard...
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_011: It always feels like you're angry or something, and I\nhave a hard time with that.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_012: Scary? Me?! I always believed Tobias to be the one\nwith the intimidating presence.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_013: And just what is frightening about my beard?
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_014: I dunno... You just freak me out... Ugh, sorry. I know\nI'm being weird.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_015: What's this? You need not cry! I have done\nnothing alarming!
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_016: This will spur false rumors that people of Saramis\nare brutish to innocent maidens...
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_017: Come! Let us withdraw for now.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_018: Agh! Where are we going? Are you gonna throw\nme into the Danann Sea?!
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_019: Hardly—I have brought you to our lavish parlor.\nNow please, don't cause such a scene.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_020: Ugh, sorry, sorry... You even gave me coffee and\npastries...
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_021: It felt like feeding a wild animal. You could scarcely\nswallow between sobs.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_022: My dad always told me to eat everything offered\nto me.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_023: He sounds like a very caring man. I am glad your\nfear seems to have abated.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_024: I'm sorry for the inconvenience... Ah, I mean,\nthank you...
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_C_025: {SetColor=Gray}She is a polite enough maiden, but my goodness...{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_001: Um, hello, Bonaventure!
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_002: Ah! Another strong greeting today. You are a\ncourageous maiden...in most respects.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_003: Oh, sorry... I mean, you are my elder, so I still feel\nthe need to be a little deferential...
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_004: Hoho. I cannot find fault with such politeness.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_005: Phew... I'm glad you're so kind.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_006: I can't help but be a little scared of the people\nfrom Saramis.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_007: I would say more than "a little," but pray continue.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_008: Well, I realized it was all just my own prejudice. All\nof you are protecting the south.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_009: Since it's so far from my own homeland, I figured it\nhad nothing to do with me.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_010: Awareness of your prejudice is remarkable in a\nmaiden of your age. Many priests cannot manage it.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_011: It gives my heart joy to know that there are those\nsuch as you outside our kingdom.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_012: Well, I don't know about all that awareness stuff...\nbut I used to want to be a priest when I was little.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_013: Except I'm not that smart. And I didn't have\nconnections or money, so I gave up on that dream.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_014: But maybe if I'd tried—if I'd knocked on the temple\ndoor—maybe I would've had a chance...
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_015: Have you considered studying?
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_016: What good would studying do at this point?
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_017: It cannot hurt. You are still young. Moreover, you are\npolite, levelheaded, and humble.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_018: If, perhaps, a bit extreme at times. Regardless, I find\none never regrets learning new things.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_019: I believe you're more clever than you credit\nyourself, Halvin.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_020: Wow... Thank you... I'm honored...
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_021: If you believe in me, then maybe I'll put in more of\nan effort to learn about the world.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_022: I mean... I've always been interested in\nlearning more.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_023: Like about...ancient stuff, amazing technology from\nthe past... Even learning about that megalith thing!
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_024: Ah! Then the storehouse of my mind may be of some\nuse to you.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_025: You may visit me whenever you wish. I shall teach\nyou all you care to learn.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_026: Thank you! I'll be extra brave and come back!
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_027: Hm? Why must you draw up the courage to visit?\nYou have nothing to worry about, I assure you.
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_028: Well, I get nervous about entering the guesthouse...\nThere were so many important people there...
MID_SE_Bon_Hal_B_029: Oh, dear Halvin...whatever will we do with you?